id: pm-beads-je7c
title: Preserve opted-in Beads extensions with versioned sidecars and explicit loss reports
description: "Acceptance: unknown nested fields survive import/export; conflicting native mappings refuse; size and privacy limits apply before mutation. Provide typed SDK and compact TOON/JSON command output, documentation and public-tracker copy validation without git."
type: Feature
status: in_progress
priority: 2
tags[1]: "gh:unbraind/pm-beads#163"
created_at: "2026-10-23T19:31:11.967Z"
updated_at: "2026-10-23T20:24:05.236Z"
author: codex-agent
acceptance_criteria: Unknown nested fields survive import/export; Conflicting native mappings refuse; Size and privacy limits apply before mutation
comments[19]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-10-23T19:31:43.910Z",codex-agent,"Overlap check against the current CLI and sibling packages: core extension custom fields provide schema-owned values; beads diff compares mapped fields, and snapshot reconciliation manages mapped fields and acknowledged bases. pm-csv owns tabular column mapping. None preserves explicitly selected opaque Beads extension objects. Design: portable schema-1 sidecar capture before ordinary import, restore after ordinary export, keyed by exact external ids. Reuse native import/export and SDK atomic file writing and host rendering; never duplicate tracker mutation, settings, locking or mappings. Reject native field selection and overlay collisions. Report every unselected extension occurrence as loss; enforce bounded JSON and privacy policy before any output write. Sidecars stay separate from tracker items and must travel with the JSONL snapshot."
  "2026-10-23T19:41:00.552Z",codex-agent,"Behavioral revert proof: disabling the restore overlay alone makes the nested-object round-trip regression fail (exit 1); disabling the native-selector guard alone makes the native-name refusal regression fail (exit 1). Restored both implementations afterward. Real compiled CLI native import/export preserved both synthetic nested extension fixtures and one dependency with no git executable available. Public-data validation archived origin/main d9b4152 into a non-git scratch tracker made read-only; all 97 public items read completely, 97 native exports, 97 synthetic nested extension fields restored, 97 deliberately unselected fields reported dropped. Source and copied tracker unchanged. Native JSONL 62639 bytes; sidecar 12087 bytes; restored JSONL 71166 bytes; compact JSON receipt 260 bytes. Native conflict, differing overlay, privacy and size refusals verified. These extension values are synthetic fixtures layered on public records, not claimed as naturally occurring source extensions."
  "2026-10-23T19:42:27.606Z",codex-agent,"All three linked checks pass via pm test --run --progress: targeted compiled-host/SDK/flag/docstring suite 15/15 (zero skipped); typecheck plus docstring lint pass; read-only public tracker validation passes. Targeted sidecar coverage is 100% lines, branches and functions. No separate lint script is defined; the repository docstring gate is the local lint check. Full npm and Bun release checks are delegated to the unchanged CI matrix as requested because host CPU is saturated. The installed host is current 2026.10.23; tracker writes use the package-pinned SDK/CLI 2026.10.20 without changing its pin."
  "2026-10-23T19:44:40.499Z",codex-agent,"Final hardening rejects unsafe integer extensions before capture to prevent JSON-number precision loss, rejects cyclic SDK envelopes with a typed refusal, and bounds existing overlay values before canonical comparison. Local health has unrelated inherited findings: a global pm-github/host pin mismatch and the already tracked installer fence drift (pm-beads-v9r1). No history repair, installer work or dependency pin changes performed. Clean CI health and npm/Bun release gates are the requested full validation authority."
  "2026-10-23T19:46:28.320Z",codex-agent,"The initial CodeQL review identified polynomial backtracking in incomplete PEM-header screening. Replaced the header regex with linear substring checks and retained the other bounded checks; added a repeated-incomplete-header fixture. SDK restore now validates typed envelopes before JSON serialization, so Infinity/NaN/unsafe integers cannot be silently coerced. Regression suite and exact-head CI are rerun after these final changes."
  "2026-10-23T19:47:23.849Z",codex-agent,"After final numeric validation and linear privacy screening, linked checks pass again: 15 targeted tests, typecheck, docstring lint, and read-only public-data validation. Sidecar source coverage remains 100% lines/branches/functions. The initial CI revision passed both npm matrix release gates; the final pushed revision must pass npm and Bun plus CodeQL before handoff. Sidecar scope is explicitly opted-in unknown top-level fields with recursively retained JSON values; nested extras inside native mapped fields remain outside this contract."
  "2026-10-23T19:50:57.503Z",codex-agent,"Verified CI on implementation commit 0bd9ab1: https://github.com/unbraind/pm-beads/actions/runs/40014208688 passed all four full release gates (npm and Bun on Node 22 and 26), each 405/405 tests with zero failures/skips and 100% measured lines/branches/functions across 10 source files. Clean CI tracker health and Bun install passed. CodeQL run https://github.com/unbraind/pm-beads/actions/runs/40014208689 passed; the initial polynomial-regex alert is fixed. PR https://github.com/unbraind/pm-beads/pull/163 is ready for review, not draft. The claim remains released and the item remains in progress for orchestrator verification. No merge or release performed. This final evidence-only tracker change will be checked again on its pushed head."
  "2026-10-23T20:00:40.378Z",codex-agent,"Review round: remote branch is current and contains main. GraphQL returned one resolved CodeQL thread, zero unresolved threads, complete thread/comment pagination, and no CodeRabbit review body or outside-diff findings. Both independent blocking findings are valid: lexical output comparison permits directory aliases, and credential key screening misses API-key spellings. Plan: canonical output/input identities before writing; normalized recursive credential screening; regressions with individual behavioral revert proofs; complete npm and Bun release gates at unchanged thresholds. No thread replies or resolutions."
  "2026-10-23T20:01:27.861Z",codex-agent,"SDK helper review: pinned sdk/mutation-guard exposes scanMutationSecrets for credential-shaped string leaves only; history-redact applies caller-supplied value matchers. Neither classifies credential key names. Keep the bounded recursive sidecar screen and normalize names by lowercasing and removing underscores/hyphens, retaining prototype-key checks. Output preflight resolves the existing parent plus basename and any existing destination symlink, compares against real input paths, and writes through the canonical parent. Cover both capture and restore inputs plus refusal preservation and non-git compiled CLI behavior."
  "2026-10-23T20:03:18.869Z",codex-agent,"Behavioral revert proofs: restoring only runSidecar from the pre-fix head, then running node --test --test-name-pattern=\"capture and restore refuse real-path\" test/sidecar.test.ts fails 0/1, exit 1, Missing expected rejection at the directory-alias capture case. Restoring only privateKey then running node --test --test-name-pattern=\"credential key normalization\" test/sidecar.test.ts fails 0/1, exit 1, Missing expected exception: api_key. Each function restored afterward; combined two-regression run passes 2/2. Full sidecar SDK/compiled non-git CLI suite passes 8/8. Targeted sidecar coverage: 100% lines, branches and functions. Self-review applied both defect classes across selectors, recursive capture, sidecar parse, SDK restore, existing overlay validation, capture destinations and both restore inputs. Regression fixtures include file symlinks, directory symlinks, missing output parents and symlink loops; source bytes remain unchanged on refusals."
  "2026-10-23T20:05:51.579Z",codex-agent,"All four initial linked checks passed: 17/17 targeted tests, typecheck/docstrings, read-only 97-record public validation and 2/2 new regressions. First isolated npm gate passed 407/407 tests, zero skips, but coverage failed at reconcile.ts:473 because the agent-exported PM_AUTHOR prevents the existing default-author branch from executing. Sidecar coverage is 100% in that run. Rerun release gates with PM_AUTHOR absent in the test environment, matching CI; keep codex-agent for tracker writes and keep every coverage threshold unchanged. No timeout occurred."
  "2026-10-23T20:07:46.270Z",codex-agent,"The isolated full npm release gate now passes with PM_AUTHOR absent from the test environment: 407/407 tests, zero failures/cancellations/skips, 100% measured lines/branches/functions across all 10 configured source files at unchanged thresholds. Fresh HOME and disabled global/system Git config reproduced CI identity. Typecheck, workflow contract, build, docstrings, production audit (zero vulnerabilities), pack dry-run, changelog check, publish attestation and changelog-date checks all passed. Full Bun gate is running next. The source dist build is refreshed but dist is ignored and not tracked by this repository."
  "2026-10-23T20:09:22.539Z",codex-agent,"Final review-round acceptance: full npm and Bun release gates both pass locally, each 407/407 tests with zero failures/cancellations/skips and 100% measured lines/branches/functions across all 10 configured source files. Exact linked gate commands: env -u PM_AUTHOR npm run release:check; env -u PM_AUTHOR bun run release:check. Both ran with fresh HOME and disabled global/system Git config. Initial npm coverage-only miss from inherited PM_AUTHOR passed after matching CI environment; no timeouts occurred and thresholds were unchanged. Typecheck, docstrings, production audit (zero vulnerabilities), build/packing, workflow/attestation/date contracts and changelog checks pass. Four earlier linked checks passed through pm test --run --progress (17 targeted tests, typecheck/docstrings, read-only 97-record measurement, two regression cases). Both individual revert proofs are recorded above. Whole-diff review and added-line privacy/append-only-history checks pass. No new pm CLI/SDK bug discovered; inherited installer-fence follow-up and local global-extension version skew remain outside scope. Claim released for orchestrator verification; item stays in progress. No thread reply/resolution, merge or release."
  "2026-10-23T20:16:19.451Z",codex-agent,"Size-boundary review round: remote head is current and includes main. Complete GraphQL thread/comment pagination returned zero unresolved threads; the sole resolved CodeQL thread PRRT_kwDOSZpl5M6vwA6- retains its linear PEM scan. All review bodies were inspected; no CodeRabbit review or outside-diff findings exist. Confirmed the independent blocker: synthetic identity JSONL inflates sidecar validation near 8 MiB. Plan direct envelope validation with shared identity and per-record limits, actual input/output byte checks, boundary regressions and behavioral revert proofs. Whole-diff self-review also found capture accepts exact-limit input whose restored terminal newline exceeds the output cap; cover this and CLI sidecar serialization consistency."
  "2026-10-23T20:19:09.027Z",codex-agent,"Implemented direct sidecar shape, identity, count, privacy, per-record extension-byte and digest validation; no synthetic JSONL reconstruction. Capture and restore share actual normalized JSONL serialization and its terminal-newline byte cap. CLI capture now writes exactly the SDK JSON bytes, removing an unvalidated extra newline. Reviewer fixture measures 8,378,349 input bytes, 8,378,064 sidecar bytes and 8,378,350 restored bytes, all below 8,388,608. Added exact-limit sidecar CLI/SDK round-trip, typed one-byte-over restored-output capture refusal, and direct-envelope invariant regressions. Sidecar SDK and compiled non-git CLI suite passes 12/12; sidecar measured lines/branches/functions remain 100%. Whole-PR diff reviewed for the same size-definition defects; earlier real-path and normalized credential fixes remain intact."
  "2026-10-23T20:19:10.066Z",codex-agent,"Behavioral revert proofs against pre-round head a1d2876: revert only validateSidecar and run node --test --test-name-pattern=\"near-limit captured records\" test/sidecar.test.ts => exit 1, 0/1 passed, unexpected size_limit during parse of the reviewer fixture. Revert only captureBeadsExtensions and run node --test --test-name-pattern=\"capture refuses restored output one byte\" test/sidecar.test.ts => exit 1, 0/1 passed, missing expected typed refusal at 8,388,609 restored bytes. Revert only runSidecar and run node --test --test-name-pattern=\"CLI capture and restore share the SDK exact\" test/sidecar.test.ts => exit 1, 0/1 passed, receipt reports 8,388,609 instead of the 8,388,608 byte cap. Each function restored in a finally block; the combined three-regression run then passes 3/3, zero skips."
  "2026-10-23T20:21:25.027Z",codex-agent,"First full release gate passed: env -u PM_AUTHOR HOME=<isolated-home> GIT_CONFIG_GLOBAL=/dev/null GIT_CONFIG_NOSYSTEM=1 npm run release:check, 411/411 tests, zero failures/cancellations/skips, 100% measured lines/branches/functions across all 10 source files at unchanged thresholds. Typecheck, build, docstrings, workflow contracts, production audit, pack dry-run, changelog and attestation/date checks all passed. No timeout or retry. The linked targeted build/SDK/compiled non-git CLI/flag/docstring command also passed 21/21 through pm test --run --progress. Rebuilt dist is ignored, with no tracked dist files. Next: remaining linked regressions/public fixture, then the Bun full gate."
  "2026-10-23T20:24:00.604Z",codex-agent,"Final size-review acceptance: both env -u PM_AUTHOR npm run release:check and env -u PM_AUTHOR bun run release:check pass, each 411/411 tests, zero failures/cancellations/skips and 100% measured lines/branches/functions across all 10 configured source files, unchanged thresholds. Both ran with fresh HOME and disabled global/system Git config on Node 24.19.0 and Bun 1.3.5; no timeout or retry. All typecheck/build/docstring, workflow, audit (zero vulnerabilities), pack, changelog and attestation/date checks pass. Linked commands run via pm test --run --progress pass: 21/21 targeted, 4/4 new boundary/invariant regressions, and 97/97 public records with synthetic extensions restored in a read-only non-git tracker. SDK/CLI actual-byte checks and all three individual revert proofs are documented above. Dist rebuilt but ignored and untracked. Added-line privacy and append-only-history checks pass."
  "2026-10-23T20:24:02.883Z",codex-agent,"Separate strict-health result: isolated pinned pm health --strict-exit --require-merge-drivers exits 1 only for merge_fence_drift:2, exactly the pre-existing installer-fence issue pm-beads-v9r1. The committed .gitattributes is byte-identical to origin/main; npm ci changes its extensions fence and that incidental change was restored. History-drift check passes. No history repair, merge-policy change, telemetry change or dependency bump. No new pm CLI/SDK defect identified. Fresh pushed-head CI and reviewer verdicts remain separate evidence; no thread replies/resolutions, merge or release. Item stays in progress and claim is released for orchestrator verification."
